2. BSP Kernel and Distros
=========================

The following table summarizes the valid Wind River Linux distros for this BSP.
'Y' in each content cell stands for supported; 'N' stands for not supported:

  +--------------+-------------+------------------+-------------------+--------------+
  | valid/distro |   wrlinux   | wrlinux-graphics | wrlinux-installer | wrlinux-tiny |
  +--------------+-------------+------------------+-------------------+--------------+
  |    valid     |      Y      |        Y         |         N         |       N      |
  +--------------+-------------+------------------+-------------------+--------------+

For the supported kernel type for this BSP, please check the TARGET_SUPPORTED_KTYPES
by running 'bitbake -e virtual/kernel | grep "^TARGET_SUPPORTED_KTYPES="'.


3. Board Specific Patches
=========================

To get a list of patches applied to the kernel specific to this BSP along with
patch descriptions use git-whatchanged on the default kernel. For example:

  $ cd tmp-glibc/work-shared/<bsp_name>/kernel-source
  $ git whatchanged v6.12/standard/base..v6.12/standard/nvidia-sdk-5.15/nvidia-soc


4. Build Instructions
=====================

Because there are lots of packages under the NVIDIA Proprietary license, they are not
able to be integrated into WRLinux product. Based on this reason, users need to build
NVIDIA BSP with network enabled environment so that these NVIDIA Proprietary packages
are able to be downloaded during building project.

Note: If users want to integrate NVIDIA Proprietary package into their own product,
      they MUST consult NVIDIA and their own legal department.

4.1 Setup BSP project with the following arguments
--------------------------------------------------

	For NVIDIA Orin AGX:
	--machine nvidia-orin-agx --distro wrlinux-graphics --dl-layers --all-layers --accept-eula=yes

4.2 Setup environment and create a build directory
--------------------------------------------------

	$ . environment-setup-x86_64-wrlinuxsdk-linux
	$ . oe-init-build-env [<build>]

4.3 Add below configurations at the end of local.conf
-----------------------------------------------------

BB_NO_NETWORK = '0'
LICENSE_FLAGS_ACCEPTED += "commercial_faad2 commercial_x264 commercial"
BUILD_NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY_PACKAGE = "1"

