4.4 Build project with below command
------------------------------------

	bitbake wrlinux-image-std-sato

After building project completely, there is a compressed package as below:
<project path>/build/tmp/deploy/images/<MACHINE>/wrlinux-image-std-sato-<MACHINE>.rootfs.tegraflash.tar.zst
It will be used to NVIDIA Orin platform in later.


5. Deploy Instructions
======================

5.1 Create Deploying Environment
--------------------------------

	Create deploying environment with below commands:

	$ mkdir nvidia-deploy
	$ cp <build output path>/wrlinux-image-std-sato-<MACHINE>.rootfs.tegraflash.tar.zst nvidia-deploy
	$ cd nvidia-deploy
	$ sudo tar --zstd -xvf wrlinux-image-std-sato-<MACHINE>.rootfs.tegraflash.tar.zst

5.2 Connect NVIDIA Orin Board with Host
---------------------------------------

Assume that the host system is Ubuntu.

For NVIDIA Orin AGX board:
Get the high quality USB Type-C cable shipped with NVIDIA Orin development kit, connect the
USB Type-C end to J40 of NVIDIA Orin AGX board, connect another end to PC host.

5.3 Force Board into Recovery Mode
----------------------------------

For NVIDIA Orin AGX board:

<1> Power off NVIDIA Orin AGX board by turning off power supply

<2> Press and hold down the Force Recovery button(S3), and then power on board by turning on power supply.

<3> (Optional) If the white LED(DS2) is not lit, press the Power button(S1).

<4> Release both buttons.

<5> Run below command on host to check whether NVIDIA Orin board enters into recovery mode successfully.

    # lsusb
    ......
    Bus 003 Device 006: ID 0955:7023 NVIDIA Corp. APX
    ......

    If the host PC detect above device, it indicates that NVIDIA Orin board enters into recovery mode successfully.

5.4 Burn images into NVIDIA Orin board
--------------------------------------

For NVIDIA Orin AGX board:

    Burn images into eMMC with below commands:

    # cd nvidia-deploy
    # sudo ./doflash.sh

    After burning completely, there will be output as below:

    ......
    [ 269.0302 ] Flashing completed
    [ 269.0302 ] Coldbooting the device
    [ 269.0307 ] tegrarcm_v2 --chip 0x23 0 --ismb2
    [ 269.0312 ] MB2 version 01.00.0000
    [ 269.0330 ] Coldbooting the device
    [ 269.0334 ] tegrarcm_v2 --chip 0x23 0 --reboot coldboot
    [ 269.0338 ] MB2 version 01.00.0000

Note: Burning time is about 20 minutes, if burning action failed, please repeat the steps in section 5.3 and 5.4.


6. Boot Instructions
====================

6.1 Boot from storage device
----------------------------

6.1.1 Boot from internal eMMC
-----------------------------

1) Connect cables and external devices to NVIDIA Orin AGX board

   For NVIDIA Orin AGX board:
   - Connect USB Type-C power supply with J24 of NVIDIA Orin AGX board.
   - Connect ethernet cable with J17 of NVIDIA Orin AGX board.
   - Connect DP monitor with J18 of NVIDIA Orin AGX board.
   - (Optional)Connect USB mouse and keyboard with J33 of NVIDIA Orin AGX board.

2) Turn on the power supply

3) Setup debug console
   - Check the debug serial port on host PC
     $ ls /dev/ttyACM*
     ttyACM0
     ttyACM1
     ttyACM2
     ttyACM3
     If there are 4 ttyACM* device nodes listed, it indicate host PC detects the debug serial port.

   - Setup debug serial port with below command:
     $ sudo minicom -s
     Enter the menu item of serial port setup, set the Serial Device as /dev/ttyACM0, and keep other
     configurations as default value.

4) Login WRLinux system
   <MACHINE> login: root
   root@<MACHINE>:~# uname -a
   Linux <MACHINE> 6.12.33-yocto-standard #1 SMP PREEMPT Fri Jun 20 01:52:55 UTC 2025 aarch64 GNU/Linux

6.2 Boot From Network
---------------------

Precondition 1: In order to boot from network environment, there must be a common DHCP server and setup
                tftp server and nfs server on their host PC.

Precondition 2: Only for NVIDIA Orin AGX platform, AGX Orin 64GB-DRAM core module(P3701-0005)+AGX Orin reference carrier board(P3737-0000).
                Because on NVIDIA Orin AGX platform(p3737-0000+p3701-0005), the UEFI firmware is not able to detect the on-board ethernet
                card, it needs to attach an USB-to-Ethernet converter to board.


6.2.1 Boot from tftp server
---------------------------

1) Deploy images on tftp server

   Copy <project path>/build/tmp/deploy/images/<MACHINE>/Image into boot directory of tftp server.
   Copy <project path>/build/tmp/deploy/images/<MACHINE>/devicetree/tegra234-p3737-0000+p3701-0005-nv-bootable.dtb
   into directory of tftp server.

2) Deploy rootfs on nfs server

   Copy <project path>/build/tmp/deploy/images/<MACHINE>/wrlinux-image-std-sato-nvidia-orin-agx.rootfs.tar.bz2
   into rootfs directory of nfs server.
   Decompress it with below command:
   tar jxvf wrlinux-image-std-sato-nvidia-orin-agx.rootfs.tar.bz2

3) Enter UEFI shell environment

   Power on board, and then press 'ESC' key continuously to enter setup menu when debug serial port outputs below content.
   **********************************************************************
   Jetson System firmware version v36.4.3 date 2023-08-09T14:18:37+00:00
   ESC   to enter Setup.
   F11   to enter Boot Manager Menu.
   Enter to continue boot.
   **********************************************************************
   Enter 'Boot Manager' menu, and then select 'UEFI Shell' item.
   Enter boot partition with below command:
   Shell> ver
   UEFI Interactive Shell v2.2
   EDK II
   UEFI v2.70 (EDK II, 0x00010000)

4) Download images from tftp server

   Enter boot partition with below command:

   For NVIDIA Orin AGX Board:
   Shell> fs3:
   FS3:\> ls
   Directory of: FS3:\
   04/05/2011  23:00 <DIR>           512  EFI
             0 File(s)           0 bytes
             1 Dir(s)

   Note: If users install SD or NVME card on board, the partition number will change.

   Apply for IP address with below command:
   FS3:\> ifconfig -s eth0 dhcp
   FS3:\> ifconfig -l

   -----------------------------------------------------------------

   name         : eth0
   Media State  : Media present
   policy       : dhcp
   mac addr     : 00:E0:4C:68:3C:10

   ipv4 address : 192.168.3.110

   subnet mask  : 255.255.255.0

   default gateway: 192.168.3.1

     Routes (2 entries):
       Entry[0]
        Subnet : 192.168.3.0
        Netmask: 255.255.255.0
        Gateway: 0.0.0.0
       Entry[1]
       Subnet : 0.0.0.0
        Netmask: 0.0.0.0
        Gateway: 192.168.3.1

   DNS server   :
        192.168.3.1

   Download images with below command:
   FS3:\> tftp <tftp server ip> <tftp boot directory>/tegra234-p3737-0000+p3701-0005-nv-bootable.dtb
   FS3:\> tftp <tftp server ip> <tftp boot directory>/Image

5) Boot system with NFS

   After downloading images from tftp server, boot system with below command:

   For NVIDIA Orin AGX platform:
   FS3:\> Image mminit_loglevel=4 console=ttyTCU0,115200 console=ttyAMA0,115200 firmware_class.path=/etc/firmware \
            fbcon=map:0 nospectre_bhb video=efifb:off console=tty0 root=/dev/nfs rw \
            nfsroot=<nfs server ip>:<nfs root path>,v3,tcp ip=dhcp bl_prof_dataptr=2031616@0x102C610000 \
            bl_prof_ro_ptr=65536@0x102C600000 dtb=./tegra234-p3737-0000+p3701-0005-nv-bootable.dtb

6.2.2 Boot from PXE server
--------------------------

About PXE boot mode, there is detailed descriptions on NVIDIA official documents, please refer to below link:
https://docs.nvidia.com/jetson/archives/r36.4.3/DeveloperGuide/SD/FlashingSupport.html#configuring-a-pxe-boot-server-for-uefi-bootloader-on-jetson
https://elinux.org/Jetson/L4T/peripheral/#PXE_boot


7. Features
===========

7.1 Power and Performance
-------------------------

7.1.1 Statistics Tool
---------------------

During development phase, it often needs to measure CPU, GPU, and memory usage status, so that make sure that SoC is able to support for
all the applications running on NVIDIA Orin platform. So, NVIDIA provides the statistics tool to show important metrics of Orin platform.

The "tegrastats" command is a tool that reports memory usage, GPU usage, CPU usage, and SOC temperature for NVIDIA Orin platform.
Run this command, It will start printing the system statistics each second. If users need to customize the tegrastats behavior, it provides
the following command-line options:

root@nvidia-orin-agx:~# tegrastats --help
Usage: tegrastats [-option]
Options:
    --help                    : print this help screen
    --interval <millisec>     : sample the information in <milliseconds>
    --cpu_per_socket <numcpu> : display only the top <numcpu> by utilization per socket (default=6)
                                applicable only for socket-based systems
    --logfile  <filename>     : dump the output of tegrastats to <filename>
    --load_cfg <filename>     : load the information from <filename>
    --readall                 : collect all stats including performance intensive stats
    --save_cfg <filename>     : save the information to <filename>
    --start                 : run tegrastats as a daemon process in the background
    --stop                    : stop any running instances of tegrastats
    --verbose                 : print verbose message

There is an example of output printed by tegrastats running on Orin AGX platform.

07-04-2025 11:05:02  RAM 4000/62846MB (lfb 14352x4MB) CPU [12%@1497,4%@1497,100%@1497,0%@1497,0%@1497,0%@1497,0%@1497,0%@1497,0%@1497,0%@1497,7%@1497,0%@1497]
EMC_FREQ 6%@2133 GR3D_FREQ 29%@[815,815] NVENC off NVDEC 40%@115 NVJPG off NVJPG1 off VIC 56%@115 OFA off NVDLA0 off NVDLA1 off PVA0_FREQ off APE 174
